.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp

# data/ is DELIBERATELY tracked. Sessions run on a disposable cloud VM, so git
# is the only persistence her record has. Privacy comes from the repository
# being private and single-member — not from holding files out of it.

/temp
# ── The dashboard, in ux/ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output and dependencies. Unanchored, so they match at any depth and keep
# working if the app moves again.
node_modules/
.next/
out/

# Credentials. NEVER commit.
#
# ux/.env.local holds the gate's account list and signing secret, written by
# ux/scripts/dashboard.mjs on first run — so a clone without it is not broken,
# just fresh. ux/config/accounts.mjs IS committed and holds no credentials: it
# only reads these. The broad .env* also catches what `vercel link` writes.
.env*

# Vercel CLI state: which project this clone is linked to. Local, not shared.
.vercel
